-- title:
--   Theorem 3.1(3), p. 5 — resolvent density 𝔤(x, y) = ℭĤ(y)(H(x) − H^[y(x)) (part 3; part 1 is theorem_3_1_1; part 2 is not formalized in this mission)
-- statement:
--   Let $E=[\mathfrak l,\mathfrak h]\cap\mathbb Z$ and let $(X,\mathbb P)$ be the Markov chain with state space $E$ generated by a Q-matrix $Q$ (not necessarily conservative) that is skip-free downward, i.e. satisfies (2.1): $Q(x,x-1)>0$ for $x>\mathfrak l$ and $Q(x,y)=0$ for $y\le x-2$. Assume all states are transient and fix a reference point $\mathfrak o\in E$. Write $G$ for the resolvent, $\zeta$ for the lifetime and $T_A$ for the first hitting time of $A$. Let $\pi$ be a positive excessive measure (the reference measure of p. 3), $\mathfrak g(x,y)=G(x,y)/\pi(y)$ the resolvent density, $\widehat G$ the resolvent of the dual chain generated by $\widehat Q(y,x)=\pi(x)Q(x,y)/\pi(y)$, and $G^{[b}$ the resolvent of the chain killed on entering $[b,\infty)$.
--
--   Define
--   $$\widehat H(y)=\lim_{x\uparrow\mathfrak h}\frac{\widehat G(y,x)}{\widehat G(\mathfrak o,x)},\qquad \mathbf H^{[b}(x)=\lim_{y\downarrow\mathfrak l}\frac{G^{[b}(x,y)}{G(\mathfrak o,y)} .$$
--   These limits exist, $G(x,y)<\infty$ for $x,y\in E$, and for $x,y\in E$
--   $$\mathfrak g(x,y)=\mathfrak C\,\widehat H(y)\big(H(x)-\mathbf H^{[y}(x)\big),\qquad \mathfrak C=\mathfrak g(\mathfrak o,\mathfrak o).\tag{3.2}$$
--
--   This expresses the whole resolvent through the three fundamental excessive functions and is the basis of every identity in Theorem 3.3.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: E = [𝔩, 𝔥] ∩ ℤ with 𝔩 < 𝔥 in ℤ ∪ {±∞} → E : Set ℤ with E.OrdConnected and two points x < y in E (𝔩 = −∞ iff ¬ BddBelow E, 𝔥 = ∞ iff ¬ BddAbove E); reason: an order-connected subset of ℤ with at least two points is exactly such an integer interval
--   - encoding: all states in E are transient → AllTransient E Q: G(x, x) < ∞ for every x ∈ E; reason: Norris, Markov Chains, Theorem 3.4.2, which the paper itself invokes on p. 3; an absorbing state has G(x, x) = ∞
--   - encoding: the Markov chain (X, ℙ) generated by Q (jump chain/holding time definition, p. 2) → transition, resolvent, hitProb, hitBeforeProb, exitDist, killedResolvent computed from jump-chain path sums with Exp(1) holding clocks; reason: this is the paper's construction (i)–(iv); the cemetery ∂ is represented by leaving E
--   - encoding: the fixed positive excessive reference measure π of p. 3 (standing for Section 3) → explicit hypotheses π : ℤ → ℝ, ∀ x ∈ E, 0 < π x, IsExcessiveMeasure E Q π; reason: the section's standing assumption written into the binders
--   - reading: H^{[b}(x) = lim_{y↓𝔩} G^{[b}(x, y)/G(𝔬, y) and Ĥ(y) = lim_{x↑𝔥} Ĝ(y, x)/Ĝ(𝔬, x), without a printed case split → value at 𝔩 (resp. 𝔥) when E is bounded below (resp. above), limit along atBot (resp. atTop) otherwise; existence of the limit asserted; reason: the paper defines the notation lim_{y↓𝔩} by this case split for H in Theorem 3.1(1)
--   - encoding: G(x, y) < ∞ for x, y ∈ E (p. 3, from transience), presupposed by the real formula (3.2) → conclusion clause resolvent E Q x y ≠ ⊤, and 𝔤 computed with .toReal; reason: the resolvent is ℝ≥0∞-valued; the clause makes .toReal faithful
-- source:
--   Loeffen, Patie, Wang, Fluctuation Theory of Continuous-Time, Skip-Free Downward Markov Chains with Applications to Branching Processes with Immigration, arXiv:2208.14425v1, p. 5, Theorem 3.1(3), (3.2); p. 3 for the reference measure π and the finiteness of G

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Chain
open scoped ENNReal Topology
open Filter MeasureTheory

namespace SkipFreeFluct.MBI

/-- Theorem 3.1(3), p. 5. Under the assumptions of Theorem 3.1, with a positive excessive
reference measure `π` (p. 3): the limits `Ĥ(y) = lim_{x ↑ 𝔥} Ĝ(y, x)/Ĝ(o, x)` (dual chain) and
`H^{[b}(x) = lim_{y ↓ 𝔩} G^{[b}(x, y)/G(o, y)` (chain killed on entering `[b, ∞)`) exist, the
resolvent is finite on `E × E`, and the resolvent density satisfies (3.2):
`𝔤(x, y) = ℭ Ĥ(y) (H(x) - H^{[y}(x))` with `ℭ = 𝔤(o, o)`. -/
theorem theorem_3_1_3 (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (hE : IsStateSpace E) (hQ : IsQMatrix E Q)
    (hS : SkipFreeDown E Q) (hT : AllTransient E Q) (o : ℤ) (ho : o ∈ E)
    (π : ℤ → ℝ) (hπpos : ∀ x ∈ E, 0 < π x) (hπ : IsExcessiveMeasure E Q π) :
    (¬ BddAbove E → ∀ y ∈ E,
      Tendsto (fun x : ℤ =>
          (resolvent E (dualQ π Q) y x).toReal / (resolvent E (dualQ π Q) o x).toReal) atTop
        (𝓝 (fundHhat E Q π o y))) ∧
    (¬ BddBelow E → ∀ b ∈ E, ∀ x ∈ E,
      Tendsto (fun y : ℤ =>
          (killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ici b) x y).toReal / (resolvent E Q o y).toReal) atBot
        (𝓝 (fundHb E Q o b x))) ∧
    (∀ x ∈ E, ∀ y ∈ E, resolvent E Q x y ≠ ⊤) ∧
    ∀ x ∈ E, ∀ y ∈ E,
      rdens E Q π x y =
        rdens E Q π o o * fundHhat E Q π o y * (fundH E Q o x - fundHb E Q o y x) := by sorry

end SkipFreeFluct.MBI
